  <!--
    DECLARED SO THE APP IS LOADED ON WEBDAV REQUESTS. This is the missing half of
    the trash-purge bug (saga §5.7), and it is invisible until you look for it.

    `register()` runs for every enabled app during bootstrap, but `boot()` only runs
    when an app is actually LOADED — and remote.php, the WebDAV entry point, loads a
    restricted set:

        $appManager->loadApps(['authentication']);
        $appManager->loadApps(['extended_authentication']);
        $appManager->loadApps(['filesystem', 'logging']);

    With no <types>, this app was never in that set, so boot() never ran on a DAV
    request. Everything wired in register() — the copy, move, rename, create and
    soft-delete listeners — kept working, which is exactly what made the gap so hard
    to see: only the ONE thing wired in boot(), the legacy trash-purge hook, was
    silently dead. A perfectly correct hook, connected in a method that never ran.

    `filesystem` is the type for apps that must be present when the filesystem is in
    play, which is what a file-event-driven mirror is.
  -->
  <types>
    <filesystem/>
  </types>
